## Platform datasources

Platform datasources are built-in sources prefixed with `_`. They fetch data from internal platform stores (e.g., activity log in MongoDB) instead of ClickHouse or external APIs.

### Naming convention

```
_platform.v<N>.<source_name>[.<time_window>]
```

- `_` prefix — identifies platform source (handled by `isPlatformSource()`)
- `platform` — namespace
- `v<N>` — schema version; bump when breaking changes to columns or behavior
- `source_name` — the resource (`activity_log`)
- `time_window` — optional parameter (`24h`, `7d`, `30d`)

### Available sources

| Source ref | Description |
|---|---|
| `_platform.v1.activity_log` | Full activity log (up to 1000 rows) |
| `_platform.v1.activity_log.24h` | Last 24 hours |
| `_platform.v1.activity_log.7d` | Last 7 days |
| `_platform.v1.activity_log.30d` | Last 30 days |

### Legacy aliases

| Alias | Resolves to |
|---|---|
| `_activity_log` | `_platform.v1.activity_log` |

### Activity log schema (v1)

| Column | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `timestamp` | TIMESTAMP | When the action was executed |
| `org_id` | VARCHAR | Organization ID |
| `user_id` | VARCHAR | User who performed the action |
| `skill_id` | VARCHAR | Skill datasource key |
| `action_id` | VARCHAR | `{source}.{operationId}` |
| `entity_type` | VARCHAR | Extracted entity type (e.g., `campaign`) |
| `entity_id` | VARCHAR | Entity ID from params |
| `action` | VARCHAR | `{source}.{operationId}` |
| `params` | VARCHAR | JSON-encoded action params |
| `source` | VARCHAR | `ui`, `mcp`, or `api` |
| `status` | VARCHAR | `executed`, `failed`, `blocked`, `cancelled` |
| `error` | VARCHAR | Error message (null on success) |
| `skill_hash` | VARCHAR | Hash of the skill definition |
| `context` | VARCHAR | Ad account ID or other context |
| `is_current_user` | BOOLEAN | Whether the action was performed by the current user |

### Usage in dashboards

```yaml
datasource: _platform.v1.activity_log.7d
```

Platform datasources require no `datasources:` definition in YAML — use the source ref directly as the widget `datasource` value.

### How it works

1. Widget references `_platform.v1.activity_log.7d` as datasource
2. Client detects the `_` prefix and sends the source ref to the server
3. Server parses the ref, queries the activity log store with the time filter, and returns Parquet
4. Parquet is loaded into DuckDB — widget queries locally as usual

